---
import Base from "../../layouts/Base.astro";
import DemoFrame from "../../components/DemoFrame.tsx";
import data from "@examples/advisory.json";
import dataZh from "@examples/advisory.zh.json";
---

<Base title="Advisory · Latent 潜 demo" description="A conversational advisory agent: the primary plane is the answer itself + the assumptions it rests on + the caveats + what still needs confirming.">
  <section class="wrap" style="padding-top:64px">
    <a class="demo-back" href="/">◂ Latent · 潜</a>
    <div class="kicker" data-i18n="en">Application demo · Advisory / recommendation (conversational)</div>
    <div class="kicker" data-i18n="zh">应用 Demo · 助手 / 建议（对话）</div>
    <h2 data-i18n="en">Tech-stack advice — should we go with K8s?</h2>
    <h2 data-i18n="zh">技术选型咨询 — 该上 K8s 吗</h2>
    <p data-i18n="en">
      The most dangerous thing in giving advice is <strong>dressing hidden assumptions up as confidence</strong>. Here the <span class="mono" style="color:var(--grounded)">answer</span> is given directly, but the <strong>assumptions</strong> it rests on are surfaced explicitly and annotated with "what would flip the conclusion"; the <span class="mono">tradeoff</span> says when the trade pays off, and the compliance <span class="mono" style="color:var(--open)">risk</span> is kept as an honest open — this is exactly what the Grounding Contract looks like in a conversation.
    </p>
    <p data-i18n="zh">
      给建议最危险的是<strong>把藏起来的假设包装成自信</strong>。这里 <span class="mono" style="color:var(--grounded)">answer</span> 直接给出，但它依赖的<strong>假设</strong>被显式亮出并标注“什么会让结论反转”，<span class="mono">tradeoff</span> 指出何时这笔交易划算，合规 <span class="mono" style="color:var(--open)">risk</span> 作为诚实的 open——这正是 Grounding Contract 在对话场景的样子。
    </p>
    <DemoFrame data={data} dataZh={dataZh} mode="scenario" stepped client:load />
  </section>
</Base>
